{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> Its meaning: this tent will not be moved; rather, HaShem will be exalted for us, in a province that has rivers around it." "<b>יאורים.</b> Defective [of] vav, like שמש ירח עמד (Habakkuk 3:11)." "<b>ידים.</b> Places, and the meaning is from every side, and they are rivers through which none will go in rowing, and the meaning is that they need not fear an enemy, neither from the sea nor from the dry land."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:35.265429414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}